  "notes": [
   "Parts are the same as in step 1, with no additions or removals.",
   "Rail mapping, from the image: tp is the top + rail (5V), tn the top - rail (GND), bp the bottom + rail (5V), bn the bottom - rail (GND). The right-hand black and red jumpers tie the top rails to the bottom rails.",
   "The catalogue puts the top half in bank t (rows a-e) and the bottom half in bank b (rows f-j). Exact hole numbers are read approximately from the image.",
   "Signal: pin 8, 100 ohm resistor (10t to 12t), speaker, then the GND rail. The 100 ohm value follows the parts list; the schematic label says 10k.",
   "Each FSR has a 5V lead (to the bottom + rail) and a signal lead to a breadboard column. That column also has the yellow wire to A0, A1 or A2 and a 10k resistor to the bottom GND rail.",
   "FSR-to-extension-wire joins are modelled as twisted lead joins; the manual does not say how they are made."
  ]
 },
